# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:9
translate plain ch1_genesis_fa35906f:

    # narrator "Day one. You badge out of BigCorp for the last time, savings account modest, group chat feral."
    narrator "Day one. You scan your badge to leave BigCorp for the last time."
    narrator "Your savings are small. Your group chat is wild with excitement."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:10
translate plain ch1_genesis_c73965f5:

    # pc "Okay. A collective. Actually collectively owned. What are we making?"
    pc "Okay. A collective. A business that we all really own together."
    pc "So what are we making?"
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Each option is a different kind of business, with its own kind of problems."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} 'Masters' are the original recordings of songs. 'Drops' are small, limited product releases."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:15
translate plain ch1_genesis_f5b84da6:

    # narrator "A label. Contracts, catalogs, and a century of artists getting robbed to learn from."
    narrator "A record label. That means contracts and catalogs of songs."
    narrator "Labels have robbed artists for a hundred years. You can learn from that history."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:19
translate plain ch1_genesis_ab88d939:

    # narrator "Streetwear. Hype is a supply chain, and supply chains are where dreams meet customs forms."
    narrator "Streetwear. Hype — excitement — is what sells it."
    narrator "But you still must make and ship real products. That's where dreams meet customs forms at the border."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:23
translate plain ch1_genesis_9e4f08c5:

    # narrator "An artist collective. The oldest idea here, wearing the newest clothes."
    narrator "An artist collective. Artists share a studio and share the profits."
    narrator "It is the oldest idea here, in new clothes."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:27
translate plain ch1_genesis_00bc31ad:

    # m "Hey. I heard you're starting something interesting."
    m "Hey. I heard you're starting something interesting."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:28
translate plain ch1_genesis_f95a4a36:

    # m "Maya. Smart contracts, tokenomics, the whole stack. I've watched too many DAOs die of idealism to be polite about it."
    m "I'm Maya. I build smart contracts — programs that run on a blockchain."
    m "I also do tokenomics, the rules for a project's tokens. I do the whole tech side."
    m "A DAO is a group owned and run by its members, using code."
    m "I've seen too many DAOs die from pure idealism. So I won't be polite about it."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:33
translate plain ch1_genesis_249feae7:

    # m "Cool. Enthusiasm noted. Now let me interrogate your governance philosophy anyway."
    m "Cool. You're excited. Noted."
    m "But I'll still ask hard questions about your governance. That means how this group makes decisions."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:37
translate plain ch1_genesis_9fad2a7c:

    # m "Correct first question."
    m "That's the right first question."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:38
translate plain ch1_genesis_7d10c639:

    # m "Decentralization is a spectrum, not a virtue. Pure democracy sounds great until your first 51%% attack. Smart governance is knowing when to decentralize."
    m "Decentralization means power is spread out, not held by one person."
    m "It's a scale, not a virtue. More is not always better."
    m "Pure democracy sounds great until your first 51%% attack. That's when someone gets over half the votes and takes control."
    m "Smart governance means knowing when to decentralize."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:42
translate plain ch1_genesis_6e70c4e3:

    # m "Before I write a single line: equity. Let's have the awkward conversation now, while we still like each other."
    m "Before I write any code, we need to talk about equity. Equity means who owns how much of the company."
    m "This talk is uncomfortable. It's easier now, while we still like each other."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} A 50/50 equal split is simple and feels fair now. It doesn't change if one person later does more. Merit-based means shares follow each person's work, but the rules stay loose for now."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Vesting means you earn your share over time. With a one-year cliff, anyone who leaves before one year gets nothing. It protects the group, but feels less trusting today."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:49
translate plain ch1_genesis_8db4ddd1:

    # m "...Sure. Feels fair today. Ask me again the month our contributions diverge."
    m "...Sure. It feels fair today."
    m "Ask me again in the month when one of us starts doing much more work."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:55
translate plain ch1_genesis_83b9f9d3:

    # m "Ambitious. 'As we go' is doing a lot of work in that sentence. Get it in writing."
    m "Ambitious. But 'as we go' is very vague. It pushes the hard part to later."
    m "Put it in writing."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:61
translate plain ch1_genesis_2ef7d98b:

    # m "You read the post-mortems. Okay. I'm in."
    m "You read the post-mortems. Those are reports on why other projects failed."
    m "Okay. I'm in."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:67
translate plain ch1_genesis_1a1e8751:

    # j "YO. Your server is blowing up! I'm Jordan — community's my thing. Tech means nothing without the people, you know?"
    j "YO. Your chat server is growing SO fast! I'm Jordan. Community is my thing."
    j "Tech means nothing without the people, you know?"

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:68
translate plain ch1_genesis_943d1c11:

    # j "Also, heads up: you already have a troll farm, two quiet quitters, and one guy with a megaphone and empty hands. It's day one. This is normal."
    j "Also, a warning. You already have a group of trolls — people who post just to cause trouble."
    j "Two members have stopped helping but never left. And one guy talks very loudly but does nothing."
    j "It's day one. This is normal."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Community first means spending time and money now on rules, trust and moderators. Growth first means getting big fast and building those systems later."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} A moat is something that protects a business from competitors."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:74
translate plain ch1_genesis_be1fe267:

    # j "Reputation, progressive trust, actual moderation. It's unglamorous and it's everything. On it."
    j "Reputation scores. Trust that people earn step by step. Real moderators."
    j "It's boring work, and it's everything. I'm on it."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:78
translate plain ch1_genesis_e44ddd9e:

    # j "Momentum's great until the first fight. Fine — but I'm writing 'I said this' in the channel topic."
    j "Speed is great until the first big fight. Fine."
    j "But I'm writing 'I said this' at the top of the channel."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:83
translate plain ch1_genesis_0bfa71a8:

    # a "I've been reading your tokenomics draft. Alex — DeFi background, treasury management."
    a "I've been reading your tokenomics draft — your plan for the tokens."
    a "I'm Alex. My background is DeFi, which means finance apps on the blockchain."
    a "I do treasury management. The treasury is the group's shared money."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:84
translate plain ch1_genesis_d0cb60dc:

    # a "You're leaving 40%% unallocated? Bold choice. ...Or reckless. Depends on your vesting schedule."
    a "You're leaving 40 percent of the tokens with no plan? Bold choice."
    a "...Or reckless. It depends on your vesting schedule — when people get their tokens."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Hiring Alex brings in a money expert, who is not cheap. Letting the community manage the money keeps control shared, with less expert help."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:90
translate plain ch1_genesis_1edbe1ac:

    # a "Smart. I'm expensive, but so is learning treasury management from Twitter threads."
    a "Smart choice. I'm expensive."
    a "But learning treasury management from Twitter posts is expensive too."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:94
translate plain ch1_genesis_4ad41ee8:

    # a "Adorable. I'll be nearby when 'the community' meets its first bear market."
    a "Cute. I'll be close by when 'the community' meets its first bear market."
    a "That's a long time when prices keep falling. Good luck."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:99
translate plain ch1_genesis_135ab5b3:

    # v "So you're the new collective. I organized unions for thirty years — we were doing 'governance tokens' in 1936. We called them union cards."
    v "So you're the new collective. I organized unions for thirty years."
    v "We had 'governance tokens' back in 1936. We called them union cards."
    v "A card gave you a vote. Same idea."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:100
translate plain ch1_genesis_db312ebb:

    # v "One question, founder: when this goes wrong — and something always goes wrong — who is legally holding the bag?"
    v "One question, founder. Something always goes wrong."
    v "When it does, who is legally responsible? Who pays the bill?"
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} A legal wrapper is an official legal form for the group, like a company. It costs 15,000 dollars now."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Without one, the law does not clearly say who is responsible for the group."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:107
translate plain ch1_genesis_d2168c73:

    # v "Boring, expensive, and correct. You may survive this industry yet."
    v "Boring, expensive, and correct."
    v "You may survive this industry after all."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:112
translate plain ch1_genesis_23f805b4:

    # v "Mm. A court once served an entire DAO through the help-desk chat box. But sure. No bag."
    v "Mm. A court once delivered legal papers to a whole DAO. It used the DAO's help-desk chat box."
    v "But sure. Nobody is responsible."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:117
translate plain ch1_genesis_f3e07d90:

    # narrator "2:47 AM. An encrypted message from an account with a hooded PFP and no history."
    narrator "2:47 AM. A secret, encrypted message arrives."
    narrator "It's from an account with a hooded PFP — a profile picture — and no history."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:119
translate plain ch1_genesis_2e91e0d0:

    # s "found a reentrancy path in your mint contract. you have not launched. this is the good timeline. voice call, camera off, or keep the bug."
    s "found a reentrancy bug in your mint contract."
    s "you have not launched yet. so this is lucky timing."
    s "voice call, camera off. or you keep the bug."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} A mint contract is the code that creates your tokens. Reentrancy is a bug that can let someone take money many times."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Spectre is a stranger with no history. You can trust them, question them, or ignore them."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:125
translate plain ch1_genesis_772b87b6:

    # s "patched. you listen. that's rarer than the bug."
    s "patched. you listened. that's rarer than the bug."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:129
translate plain ch1_genesis_006f2d2c:

    # s "someone who reads bytecode for fun. wrong question, but i fixed it anyway. next time ask 'what did you find.'"
    s "someone who reads bytecode for fun. raw machine code."
    s "wrong question. but i fixed it anyway."
    s "next time ask 'what did you find.'"

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:133
translate plain ch1_genesis_1b73ca3a:

    # narrator "The account goes quiet. The bug does not."
    narrator "The account goes quiet. The bug does not go away."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:137
translate plain ch1_genesis_f4dac308:

    # narrator "Token design ceremony. This shapes everything that follows."
    narrator "Token design time. You decide who gets the tokens."
    narrator "This choice shapes everything that follows."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} Equal split: the founders get the same amount. Merit-based: more tokens for more work, so someone must measure the work."
    narrator "{color=#578C88}TIP:{/color} 60 percent to the treasury: most tokens go to the shared community fund, and less to the founders."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:141
translate plain ch1_genesis_6cab295d:

    # narrator "Clean, simple, and — as Maya mutters — 'a tie waiting for a breaker.'"
    narrator "Clean and simple. But Maya says quietly that it's 'a tie waiting for a tie-breaker.'"
    narrator "With two equal owners, nobody has the final say in a disagreement."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:144
translate plain ch1_genesis_da8f1f5b:

    # narrator "Fair in theory. The spreadsheet measuring 'contribution' becomes the most political document you own."
    narrator "Fair in theory."
    narrator "But someone must track each person's 'contribution' in a spreadsheet."
    narrator "That spreadsheet becomes the most fought-over document you own."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:148
translate plain ch1_genesis_302b8f74:

    # narrator "The community cheers. Alex does math quietly, like a person at a funeral."
    narrator "The community cheers. Alex quietly does the math."
    narrator "Alex looks as serious as a person at a funeral."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:149
translate plain ch1_genesis_e2afd614:

    # narrator "Mint night. Donations trickle in — then one address deposits more than everyone else combined."
    narrator "Mint night — the night your tokens are created. Small donations come in slowly."
    narrator "Then one address, one single wallet, puts in more than everyone else together."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:151
translate plain ch1_genesis_f7865034:

    # w "Consider it a vote of confidence. I admire builders."
    w "Consider it a sign that I believe in you. I admire builders."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:153
translate plain ch1_genesis_6370f03b:

    # narrator "The tokens never move again. They sit there. Waiting. (You will think about this later.)"
    narrator "Those tokens never move again. They just sit there. Waiting. (You will think about this later.)"

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:157
translate plain ch1_genesis_511bf257:

    # narrator "The Genesis Block is complete. Your collective is born."
    narrator "The Genesis Block is complete. That's the very first block of a blockchain."
    narrator "Your collective is born."

# game/ch1_genesis.rpy:158
translate plain ch1_genesis_69398b2b:

    # narrator "The real challenges are just beginning."
    narrator "The real challenges are only starting."

